--TEST--
A shape key `Core\Db::open` requires and the settings object omits is refused at the call, because `rule:core-api/shape-flattens-at-the-abi` flattens a key into an argument and a missing one is a call an argument short — E0402
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `driver` is the one key *both* arms of `Db\Settings` require, so it is the
// one key no literal can omit whichever arm it selects. The four written here
// are the server arm's, and that is the arm `rule:core-api/shape-arms-are-disjoint` selects — so the help
// names what that form requires rather than the merged list's single key, which
// is the sharper answer arm selection buys: the keys a caller is short of are
// the keys of the form they were evidently writing.
Core\Db::open({
    host: "db.example.test",
    database: "shop",
    user: "app",
    password: "hunter2",
});
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0402]: this member requires the shape key `driver`
   --> %s:8:15
   |
 8 | Core\Db::open({
   |               ^... `driver` is not given
   | (continues to line 13)
   = help: the keys this member requires are: driver, host, database, user, password

error: aborting due to 1 error
